{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794426414,"nonce":"M8jFsr7xmOGtRxa7ViaauRx7LK0=","title":"x","message":"Found 2026-11-12 by a review of the ADR-0018 amendment. Read from the code; not reproduced.\n\n`build.context` and `build.dockerfile` are not validated. The executor passes them to buildctl as given (`--local context={context}`, `--local dockerfile={context}`, `filename={dockerfile}`, crates/scarab-executor-k8s/src/lib.rs:5713-5717), and the Pipeline check for a build step looks only at `image` (crates/scarab-pipeline/src/lib.rs:5561-5583). The registry credential is mounted in the same container at `/scarab/registry` (lib.rs:5678).\n\nSo `context: /scarab/registry` makes the mounted dockerconfigjson the build context. A Dockerfile can `COPY config.json` and `RUN` a command that sends it out. Any absolute path in the build container works the same way.\n\n`image` has the same gap in another form: it is written into `--output type=image,name={image},push=…`, which buildctl reads as comma-separated `key=value`, so an `image` containing `,` adds output options.\n\nCombined with the fork-PR ticket filed beside this one, a fork PR can read the org's `REGISTRY_AUTH` or the GitHub App's `packages: write` token.\n\nAlso likely, not tested: BuildKit runs with `--oci-worker-no-process-sandbox` (lib.rs:4669-4673). BuildKit's docs say build containers can then kill and possibly ptrace the daemon, so a `RUN` step may reach the outer container's files without any context trick. If so, path validation narrows the hole but does not close it, and the credential should not be in the build container at all (mint into a file only buildctl's auth reads, or push from a second container).\n\nFix:\n1. `context` and `dockerfile`: workspace-relative, no leading `/`, no `..` component, checked at compile time and again at launch.\n2. `image`: an OCI image reference with no `,` (reuse `oci::is_image_reference`).\n3. Check whether a `RUN` step can read `/proc/\u003cpid\u003e/root/scarab/registry`; file a follow-up with what it finds.\n\nApplies to the `build` kind today and to `lib:thulasi-ram/build` after ADR-0018's 2026-11-12 amendment: the library must validate the same inputs.","files":null}]}